    explanation: 'Protein C (and S) have the shortest half-lives among vitamin-K factors, so warfarin transiently lowers the anticoagulant arm FIRST — a hypercoagulable window causing microvascular thrombosis in skin fat. That is why therapeutic heparin must bridge the first 4–5 days of warfarin.',
